findings:
Code from outside the pin's tree ships under 1ee778a4 and passes gradle, through an environment CFLAGS (pre-existing, but it contradicts the new docs) [M]. Input: a pinned additive build of a clean clone at the pin, with CFLAGS='-include <scratch>/inject.h' in the environment; the header defines one retained string.
Observed:
- 'pin = met' and 'export verified: ... 8 trees ..., 232 files ...';
- the -include on 76 compile lines in luajit_build.log, and 76 of 77 LuaJIT objects differing from build/native's (lj_opt_mem.o 228dc3d4, canonical 42bd49f9);
- the string present in the DLL, stamp 1ee778a4|LuaJIT 2.1.ROLLING|412be694, collected into dist;
- gradle verifyModAssets rc 0 ('native fingerprint names the pinned LuaJIT commit 1ee778a4').
Cause [S]: these variables are used in LuaJIT's src/Makefile and never assigned, so they come from the environment: CFLAGS, LDFLAGS, LIBS, CROSS, PREFIX, MULTILIB, LMULTILIB, INSTALL_LJLIBD, HOST_CFLAGS, HOST_LDFLAGS, HOST_LIBS, TARGET_CFLAGS, TARGET_FLAGS, TARGET_LDFLAGS, TARGET_LIBS, TARGET_SHLDFLAGS (exp/used.txt against exp/assigned.txt). MAKEFLAGS and MAKEFILES can also set make variables [I]. A common developer setting such as CFLAGS=-march=native would reach a release build the same way [I].
Minimal fix, not measured: pass all of those empty on the make command line at :1245 (empty is the canonical value: nothing currently sets them), unset or refuse MAKEFLAGS, MAKEFILES and GNUMAKEFLAGS, and refuse gcc's CPATH, C_INCLUDE_PATH, GCC_EXEC_PREFIX and COMPILER_PATH. Then rerun W1.
